xnu-12377 2001: the ios-sweet iOS 16 drivers (xnu/patches 0081-0247 as ported to 12377: Adreno 618 GPU + native
Metal render client, RPMh/BCM votes, pmem, BT, haptics, audio, sensors, baseband/IPA, charger, battery fixes) on
top of Bergamota's series + 2000. Made as a git merge of the port branch (x12377 + our 144 cherry-picks; 0167/0248
deferred, scheduler hunks of 0177-0179 dropped) into Bergamota 37a7a7a + 2000, then `git diff`.

Merge decisions (Bergamota kept where it already runs iOS 26 on sweet):
 - Bergamota: sweet_usb.c (+ our sweetfiles hook), SweetSurface.cpp (iOS 26 plane ABI), SweetFramebuffer.cpp,
   HID touch mapping, keystore wrap/unwrap, sweet_spmi.c (ours appended: sweet_spmi_write_sm6150, panel reset GPIO).
 - Ours: sweet_rpmh.c (+ Bergamota's lookup / arc_vote / rfclk_enable as compat for their Poco F1 drivers),
   the PM6150 charger as sweet_charger_pm6150.c (Bergamota's sweet_charger.c is PMI8998, beryllium-gated).
 - IOAcceleratorES is defined once (Bergamota's stub in SweetFramebuffer.cpp, not published when sweetmtl is set;
   our AGXAccelerator derives from it). Bergamota's A630 alias class is SweetA630AGXUserClient.
 - Our BT HCI exports are sweet_bt_hci_*. RedwoodWLAN.cpp / MiniIONetworkStack.cpp are not built (Bergamota's
   SweetNetwork.cpp owns IONetworkStack/IONetworkInterface/IO80211Controller); 0179's tap mark is a no-op.
Not yet: our display path (flip / GPU present copy / panel power), Wi-Fi IOKit face, scheduler (0167/0248).
GPU stays off unless sweetgpu=N (as on iOS 16).
CI fixes (run 43547351307): <stdint.h> in kernel headers, vm/vm_kern_xnu.h in sweet_pmem.c, one skywalk table, one
cpufreq copy (2000's; 0200 dark-clock hook is a no-op). sweet board: sweet_reboot.c (IMEM 0x146aa000 + PON reason +
PSCI reset, so `sweetreboot fastboot` works), Wi-Fi en0 published through sweet_net_publish_wlan (SweetNetwork.cpp).

